# 6. Relationship With Other DBMS Concepts

MySQL concepts are strongly connected:

```text
Table
 │
 ├── Primary Key
 │       ↓
 │   Clustered Index
 │
 ├── Secondary Index
 │       ↓
 │   Faster Lookup
 │
 ├── Transaction
 │       ↓
 │     ACID
 │
 ├── MVCC
 │       ↓
 │  Concurrent Reads
 │
 └── Query Optimizer
         ↓
    Execution Plan
```

This is where advanced interviews become interesting.

For example:

> **Why does the primary key affect secondary indexes in InnoDB?**

Because InnoDB's secondary index records contain the primary-key value used to locate the corresponding clustered-index record. Consequently, a large primary key increases the size of secondary indexes. ([MySQL Developer Zone][4])

