# 9. Natural Language Breakdown

Think of an index like a **book index**.

Without an index:

```text
Row 1 → check
Row 2 → check
Row 3 → check
...
Row 1,000,000 → check
```

With an appropriate index:

```text
Search Index
     ↓
email = X
     ↓
B+ Tree
     ↓
Target location
     ↓
Row
```

But an index isn't free.

Every `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, and `DELETE` may require index maintenance. Excessive indexes therefore consume storage and increase write overhead. ([MySQL Developer Zone][6])

