# 12. Tricky & Edge Cases

## Composite Index

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_user
ON users(age, name, email);
```

Conceptually:

```text
(age, name, email)
```

is **not equivalent** to:

```text
(age)
(name)
(email)
```

The ordering matters.

This leads to the famous:

### ⭐ Leftmost-prefix concept

For:

```text
(age, name, email)
```

the index can potentially support access patterns beginning with:

```text
age
age + name
age + name + email
```

But an isolated predicate on `email` doesn't provide the same straightforward leading-column access.

