# 18. Common Candidate Mistakes

### ❌ Mistake

> "Index makes every query faster."

### Better

> "Indexes can reduce the cost of locating qualifying rows, but they introduce storage and write-maintenance overhead, and the optimizer may choose a scan when that is estimated to be cheaper."

---

### ❌ Mistake

> "MySQL stores everything in the index."

### Better

Understand:

```text
InnoDB
 │
 ├── Clustered Index
 │      ↓
 │   Row data
 │
 └── Secondary Index
        ↓
     Secondary key
        +
     Primary key
```

InnoDB indexes are B-tree structures, with index records stored in leaf pages; the default InnoDB index page size is 16 KB. ([MySQL Developer Zone][7])

---

### ❌ Mistake

> "MVCC means there are multiple copies of every row forever."

Incorrect.

InnoDB uses undo information to reconstruct earlier versions for consistent reads, while old versions are eventually purged. Secondary-index version handling differs from clustered-index handling. ([MySQL Developer Zone][8])

